        <mxCell id="f3" value="GELU" style="rounded=0;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#5B6472;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontColor=#3C4350;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1046" y="803" width="62" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fx" value="x" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#3C4350;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#3C4350;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1124" y="843" width="34" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f4" value="1 × 1&lt;br&gt;conv" style="rounded=0;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#5B6472;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontColor=#3C4350;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1174" y="832" width="62" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fann" value="C → 2.66 C → C" style="text;html=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#3E4652;whiteSpace=wrap;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="927" y="920" width="240" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pb" value="(b) Inside one Transformer block" style="text;html=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#3C4350;whiteSpace=wrap;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="22" y="986" width="700" height="32" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap" value="Figure 2. Restormer never lowers the input to a fixed patch grid: a 3 × 3 convolution embeds the degraded image into 48 channels and a four-level encoder-decoder follows, holding 4, 6, 6 and 8 Transformer blocks and 1, 2, 4 and 8 attention heads from level 1 to level 4. The tapering silhouette is the spatial resolution; the bold number under each stage is the channel count. Downsampling is a 3 × 3 convolution followed by a pixel-unshuffle and upsampling by a pixel-shuffle, so resolution changes without pooling. Encoder features are concatenated at every decoder level (grey plate); a 1 × 1 convolution then halves the channels at levels 3 and 2, but level 1 has no such convolution, which is why decoder 1 and the four refinement blocks run at 96 channels rather than 48. The input image is added back after the last 3 × 3 convolution. Inside a block, LayerNorm is bias-free or with-bias by option; MDTA takes the attention across channels, so the map is (C/h) × (C/h) rather than HW × HW and cost is linear in pixels; GDFN expands by 2.66, then gates one half of the features with a GELU on the other half. Every module is [trainable] and the repository trains end to end with an L1 loss. Source: basicsr/models/archs/restormer_arch.py at commit 68dc6ac." style="text;html=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#3C4350;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="22" y="1034" width="1348" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lgbg" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#DFE3E8;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" vertex="1" parent="legend"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1160" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lgl0" value="" style="html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#C0392B;strokeWidth=2.2;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" edge="1" parent="legend"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="10" y="22" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="40" y="22" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
